    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83600.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 73,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. So there's a lot to say about why. And by the way, I've kind of heard everybody plays Matt Gates's floor speech, but nobody's playing mine. It makes me wonder what happened to my floor speech. It kind of hurts. But that's OK. So I gave a floor speech for seven and a half minutes yesterday outlining it. And I actually probably got it gone off for 20 minutes more. But let's just cover a few basics. Number one. Um, why are we in where we are? So why are we getting ready to do? Why did we do another CR? And that's what Kevin's talking about. They voted against the CR that did this that. Well, first of all, a lot of the stuff that he's talking about was so stuff. Uh, so when he says, Oh yeah, they voted against border security. No, I did. I voted against, I voted for border security and HR2. Not only did I vote for border security, I wrote most of those bills, those eight bills that went into HR2 at one time or another since I've been in Congress and they just got put into one. So that was HR2, but he actually weakened HR2 and put that in a CR and said, if you want to do this, we're gonna create this narrative. That's what they were trying to do is create a narrative. The second thing is, Earlier three days before we did that his CR with the faux HR two in it. We all voted on a Department of Homeland Security bill. And the reason I bring that up is because. We should have had those bills done last June. That's what we're required to under law. And if we would have done that, there's nobody that's getting jammed at the end. But he is part of the, he's lived kind of like in the uni party. This is what I predicted would happen last November, December, and January. I said, he will go to the Democrats ultimately to get his votes because that is what he has always done. So you get jammed on the appropriations bills. In the meantime, our national debt increased by $2 trillion. Our structural deficit is $2 trillion. Our interest into our budget is $700 billion plus. That's happened since he became the speaker. Now he'll say, well, wait, it's not me, it's the Biden administration. But you know what you could have done, and I raised this on the floor yesterday. You have the budget, and if you would have done the 12 bills, that's when the founders basically said you have the leverage, you have the check. The check is the checkbook for the House against the executive branch, even against the Senate. But he didn't use it. He didn't use it because he's part of the Uniparty. And so when he also came in and said, he implied that some of us were saying we were in places we weren't. I was there. I really was there when I watched them negotiate from $1 trillion in national debt growth over eight months to $2 trillion to $1.5 trillion. I was there for that. Well, how do I know I was there? Because I watched it. Not only that they called me and asked me to come in and to try to solve some people's problems. And myself and one of the lawyers for the committee, we wrote the language to solve those people's problems in the debt ceiling stuff, even though I said, I'm not supportive of this. But those people, they had some legitimate concerns. And what did he come back with? Benny, he came back after negotiating. He negotiated with Biden and the Senate and he came back and said, all right, we're not going to have an eight month debt ceiling lift. We're going to lift it past the 2024 election into January 2025. Yeah. So it will not be an issue. So Donald Trump, the Republican nominee, will not even be able to argue about the profligate spending or the increase in the national debt because he took it off the table. And not only did he take it off the table, he took the cap off. That's what he did. And so when people say, well, you know, what's so bad about that? Oh, I don't know. How about the existential crisis we have? How about the inflation you're feeling everywhere? How about the failure to use the purse to enforce the border or enforce energy policy changes or enforce, you know, stopping the weaponization of the DOJ against the American people? How about this simple thing? Stop funding the government that is attacking the American people.",
