    "turn_text": "deal with other people. He never made a deal with me. I've never claimed he made a deal with me. But his veracity with me, personally, on other issues here before he ran for speakers. One of the reasons I ran for speaker, and I told him this, is because he had been untruthful to me multiple times. And I know my colleagues are saying that he violated the deal. They've told me what their deal was, and he did violate that deal, not the least of which was 12 single-subject appropriations bills consistent with the Budget Control and Impound Act of 1974, which he violated. He was going to bring a couple of bills to the floor, a term limit bill and a balanced budget bill. Those were supposed to be brought to the floor. They were never brought to the floor. He said, but the term limit didn't pass out of judiciary. Well, I happen to be sitting in an impeachment inquiry hearing. I could not leave to go to that particular judiciary committee hearing at that time and vote. And, but you can always bring it up again. And if you would see, when you bring it up nine months into the whole enchilada, maybe what you should have done is go back to the first time you add some salsa to your enchilada, which would have been January and bring those bills up. He didn't do it, Benny, he didn't do it because he didn't want to do it. And so that's why they say he didn't keep promises to them.",
