    "turn_text": "Yeah, you might be able to, but here's our problem again. And I'm with you. I mean, I mentioned this on the floor yesterday. You've given 130 billion dollars to Ukraine. Yeah. You will secure your own borders. Yes. All the things you just said. But here's what you've got. The Uniparty again, I keep bringing it back. Trump was right. The swamp is real. I didn't believe it. I came into office at the same time. Trump did. I'd done work at the UN. I thought the UN was the most corrupt. I told you this before. I thought the UN was the most corrupt institution in the world until I came to the United States. Congress is like, oh, hold our beer, you know what I mean? Here's the deal. What goes on here is this notion that the unit party is going to, they want control and power. The lobby is there. They want control and power. People actually campaigned when I was running against McCarthy. People stood up in conference and said, it should be McCarthy because he raises far more money than anybody else. That's what they think is leadership, I guess. So when we start talking about, can you strip the Ukraine funding out? You got the Democrat Warhawks, and you got the neocons in the Republican Party, and they come together and they say, Oh, as long as it takes, as much as it takes. And we're just going to keep pouring money in there. You know how many dakas on the Black Sea coast can Zalinski build? I mean, for Mercy Sakes, it's enough. It is enough. And so I introduced amendments to get to pump it out. They finally had to take it out. Marjorie Taylor Greene helped get it out. Gates helped get it out, some of the same knuckleheads that are pariahs in our party and apparently, we got that funding and people were coming to me, but Andy, it's only 300 million. What's wrong with you, Andy? It's only 300 million. It's only 300 million, right? It doesn't even fill in the dot in the trillion dollar decimal point. I get all that, you know, but the bottom line is you've got to start thinking of America's Citizens first, you have to start taking care of them. So that's a long way of an eranting type of way to say, Benny. We're fighting an uphill battle, no matter who the speaker is. But I tell you what, if you have the right speaker, the right speaker can go into those people and say, this is no longer acceptable. We gave them a bunch of money. We're not going into a forever war. We're pulling back out. We're done. And that speaker would get the votes. But you have to have the courage. You have to have the communication. And you have to basically sit down with everybody. You can't just say, I'm gonna sit down with my lieutenants who tell me I'm wonderful and sit down with the K Street lobbyists who are by the way, are making money hand over fist in places like Ukraine.",
